      "font size" : 9.7,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "1) rate of wood residue application: 0, 45, 90 and 135 Mg/ha, and",
      "kids" : [ ]
    }, {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 53.203, 566.214, 255.63, 649.056 ],
      "font" : "Arial",
      "font size" : 9.7,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "2) rate of nitrogen fertilization: 0, 2.5, 5.0 and 7 .5 kg of N/Mg of wood residue in residue-amended treatments; the nonresidue amended treatment received 0, 112, 224 and 336 kg N/ha, which was equivalent to the rates of N applied on the 45 Mg/ha wood rate treatment.",
      "kids" : [ ]
    } ]
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 63,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 32.0, 432.667, 273.0, 554.0 ],
    "font" : "Arial",
    "font size" : 9.7,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Initial results indicated that while vegetation was significantly stimulated by the lowest rates of N fertilization, little subsequent difference in plant response existed among the 3 rates of N application (Smith et al 1985). For the purposes of the present analysis, therefore, plant responses to non-N fertilization will be compared to the average of responses among the 3 N fertilization rate treatments (i.e., a non-N vs. N-fertilized treatment coi'nparison)."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 66,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 33.0, 361.0, 272.667, 422.333 ],
    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "Two mixtures   of seeded species {native and introduced perennial  grasses) were sown on the site in 1981 to comprise a seed mix treatment (Smith et al 1985) . This report will present only responses of the native mixture, since this mix was later   selected to receive the gypsum treatments because  of better overall   response to the initial spoil amendments. The native mixture included 5 cool-season perennial grasses ('Rosana' western wheatgrass, Aqropyron smithii; 'Critana' thickspike wheatgrass, A. dasystachyum; Revenue'  slender wheatgrass, A: trachycaulum; Sodar'  streambank wheatgrass, 4 riparium; and 'Lodorm green needlegrass, Stipa viridula) and one shrub (Nuttall saltbush, Atriplex uttallii) . This mixture was seeded at rates to yield 130 live seedslm? for each grass   species and 32 live   seedslm? for Nuttall saltbush."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 67,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 33.333, 320.0, 252.84, 350.0 ],
    "font" : "Arial,Bold",
    "font size" : 7.4,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Table 1. Pre•treatment characteristics of bentonite spoils at ~Upton, Wyoming study site, 1981 (from Smith et al. 1985)."
